# yt-dlp.pin — the ONE place the media-tools pack's binary is named.
# yt-dlp is ~18 MB of standalone Windows executable (it carries its own
# Python), so it is not committed: tools/build-payload.sh downloads exactly
# this release, checks it against the sha256 below, and only then copies it
# into the payload as vendor/yt-dlp/yt-dlp.exe (packs.js "media-tools").
# A download that is missing or hashes differently stops a release cut, the
# same way build-dist.sh stops on a full disk. No test needs the binary.
#
# Licence: Unlicense (public domain) — https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp
# To bump, take BOTH lines from the release's own checksum file:
#   curl -L https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/releases/download/<version>/SHA2-256SUMS
# and re-cut + re-verify the installer on the VM (a new binary is a new file
# for Defender's FastPath to flag).
YTDLP_VERSION=2026.08.19
YTDLP_EXE_SHA256=66674953fe251b89f4d08c5f0e35e0728679bd67ab3d7d05c0562af101dd3e7a
